  "title": "France's Student Protests Escalate with Violence, Over 200 Arrested",
  "summary": "Violent clashes and looting broke out in France as over 200 students and staff were arrested following student protests over education cuts and staff shortages, turning school blockades into violence and causing widespread disruption.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "France's student protests over education cuts and staff shortages have escalated into violent clashes, with authorities reporting over 200 arrests and 164 police officers involved in the conflict.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Demonstrations have turned school blockades into violence, affecting over 1,000 schools across the country.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The protests have spilled over to Italy and Portugal, with rioters clashing with police and setting property on fire in Milan and Lisbon",
